lesson: 176
title: Which row? Steps that grow by the same number
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When each row has the same number more than the row before, row N has the first row plus N - 1 steps.
explain: To find which row has a certain number, take away the first row, divide by the step, and add 1.
explain: Row 1 has 8 seats and each row has 3 more. Which row has 29 seats? 29 - 8 = 21, 21 / 3 = 7 steps, so row 7 + 1 = 8.
vars: a=name f=5..20 d=2..6 r=5..15
let: v = f + (r - 1) * d
answer: r
exercise: In a hall the first row has {f} seats, and each row has {d} seats more than the row in front of it. Which row has {v} seats?
exercise: {a} saves {f} dollars in the first week and each week {d} dollars more than the week before. In which week does {a.he} save {v} dollars?
exercise: The numbers {f}, {f+d}, {f+2*d}, {f+3*d}, … go on, always growing by {d}. In which place in the list is the number {v}?
exercise: A tower of cans has {v} cans in the bottom row. Each row going up has {d} cans fewer, and the top row has {f} cans. How many rows does the tower have?
exercise: On day 1 {a} runs {f} laps, and every day {d} laps more than the day before. On which day does {a.he} run {v} laps?
exercise: A stadium has {f} seats in its first row and {d} more seats in each next row. The last row has {v} seats. How many rows are there?
test: {a} reads {v} pages on the last day of {a.his} holiday. On the first day {a.he} read {f} pages, and each day {d} pages more than the day before. How many days did the holiday last?
test: Fence posts are numbered {f}, {f+d}, {f+2*d} and so on, each number {d} bigger than the one before. The last post has the number {v}. How many posts are there?
test: Row by row a garden bed has {d} tulips more than the row before it; the first row has {f}. Which row is the one with {v} tulips?
test: A staircase of blocks: the top step uses {f} blocks, and every step below uses {d} more. The bottom step uses {v} blocks. How many steps are there?
exercise: Which row has {v} seats? The first row of a theatre in New York has {f} seats, and every row has {d} more seats than the one before.
exercise: {a} in Alberta puts {f} dollars in a piggy bank in week 1, and each week {d} dollars more than the week before. In which week does {a.he} put in {v} dollars?
exercise: A list starts at {f}, and each number is {d} greater than the last. What is the position of {v} in the list?
exercise: First row: {f} chairs. Each next row: {d} chairs more. Which row has {v} chairs?
exercise: {a} trains for a race in Cardiff: {f} minutes on the first day, and every day {d} minutes longer than the day before. On which day does {a.he} train for {v} minutes?
exercise: A pile of logs has {f} logs in the top row and {d} more logs in every row below. The bottom row has {v.words} logs. How many rows are in the pile?
exercise: In a stadium in Perth row one has {f} seats, and each next row has {d} seats more. In which row are there {v} seats?
exercise: A garden in Kent has {f} roses in its first bed, and every bed after it has {d} roses more than the bed before. Which bed has {v} roses?
test: Counting up from {f} in steps of {d}, {a} reaches {v}. How many numbers has {a.he} said, counting {f} and {v}?
test: Each floor of a parking garage in Chicago has {d} more spaces than the floor below; the ground floor, floor 1, has {f}. On which floor are there {v} spaces?
test: {a}'s savings jar gets {f} cents on the first day and {d} cents more each day than the day before. On which day does {a.he} put in {v} cents?
test: A choir in Belfast stands on steps: {f} singers on the first step and {d} more on each step behind it. The back step has {v} singers. How many steps are there?
test: How many rows does a pyramid of oranges in a shop in Christchurch have, if the top row has {f}, each lower row has {d} more, and the bottom row has {v}?
test: A sequence begins with {f} and grows by {d} at every step. Which term of the sequence is equal to {v}?
exercise: first row {f} seats, every row {d} more than the one in front. which row's got {v}
exercise: {a} saves {f} bucks week 1, {d} more each week. which week does {a.he} put away {v}
exercise: row 1 has {f} chairs, each row {d+1} more — no wait, {d} more. which row has {v} chairs
exercise: {a} reads {f} pages first day, then {d} more each day than the day before (book's like 500 pages lol). what day does {a.he} read {v} pages
test: Sam says it's row {v} lol. nah. first row {f} seats, {d} more each row, which row really has {v}?
test: {a} does {f} push-ups day 1, {d} more every day. what day's {a.he} hit {v}?
test: {a} gets {f} stickers on day one n {d} more each day than the day before, mum gave 3 extra on sunday but ignore that. which day does {a.he} get {v}
exercise: After Dad was let go, {a} starts saving: {f} dollars in the first week and {d} dollars more each week than the week before. In which week does {a.he} save {v} dollars?
exercise: old lady downstairs passed away and left a bloody mountain of tins. we stack 'em: {f} in the top row, every row {d} more than the one above. which row's got {v} tins
test: The lawyer of the late Mr Stone pays the gardener {f} dollars in the first month, raising the pay by {d} dollars every month. In which month is the gardener paid {v} dollars?
exam: In an auditorium the first row contains {f} seats, and each subsequent row contains {d} seats in excess of the row immediately preceding it. Determine the ordinal number of the row containing {v} seats.
exam: It is given that {a} deposits {f} dollars in the first week and, in each week thereafter, a sum exceeding that of the preceding week by {d} dollars. Ascertain the number of the week in which the sum deposited amounts to {v} dollars.
exam: A sequence of terms commences with the value {f}, each term exceeding its predecessor by {d}. State the position in the sequence occupied by the term whose value is {v}.
exam: Whereas a runner covers {f} laps on the first day of training and, on each subsequent day, {d} laps more than on the day preceding, determine on which day, by its number, the runner covers {v} laps.
